CL 1
L laya-3d v1 -- Native 3D adapters for the shared Scene core; no training
-- @proof {"id":"laya.frozen-cpu-floor","claim":"Default System-1 transformer retains at least 138/231 on JevBench dataset dc3995d8ae1e2fc8e81ce38431add509eb8bb39b85aadfd0c7c32079382dde51, all 93 retained value/probability outputs unchanged and layout 48/48. The floor runner exits nonzero on regression. Live browser calls alone use the admitted g3-c2 runtime and retain verified-episode confidence semantics.","checkedAt":["scripts/laya3d_regression.py:admission","grant_agent.laya_app_service.main","grant_agent.laya_service.browser_decide"],"impact":["frozen System-1 default","browser.decide/page_done","release floor exit status"],"phase":"post"}
A scene.transcribe(domain:str, source:object) -> scene -- Exact private game-dev Edit session; native facts
A laya.judge(scene:object) -> verdict -- Shared crisp predicates and scoped instant episodes
A scene.improve(domain:str, source:object, budget:object) -> receipt -- Shared strict finding reduction and guarded metrics; restore rejected revisions
P inspect(domain, source): scene.transcribe(domain, source)
P upgrade(domain, source, budget): scene.improve(domain, source, budget)
P image-to-model(source, budget): scene.improve("laya3d", source, budget)
A shape.primitive(args:object) -> mesh -- box sphere cylinder cone
A shape.extrude(args:object) -> mesh -- observed outline loops with holes; declared depth
A shape.lathe(args:object) -> mesh -- radial profile around Z
A shape.sweep(args:object) -> mesh -- elliptical cross sections with capped ends
A shape.boolean(args:object) -> mesh -- exact union difference intersection
A shape.mirror(args:object) -> mesh -- native axis mirror
A shape.bevel(args:object) -> mesh -- bounded bevel
A shape.subdivide(args:object) -> mesh -- bounded native subdivision
A shape.displace(args:object) -> mesh -- provided depth image as UV displacement; eyes only
A shape.visual_hull(args:object) -> mesh -- carve bounds with observed masks through fitted weak-perspective cameras (hull_math)
A shape.smooth(args:object) -> mesh -- voxel remesh at hull pitch plus bounded relaxation
A shape.project_texture(args:object) -> mesh -- per-face source-view colour through the fitted cameras; occlusion not modelled; alpha never hides geometry errors
